**/Debug/
**/debug/
# Exception: this is game content (debug-only launch stages/scripts), not
# a CMake Debug/Release build-output directory - the **/debug/ rule above
# is aimed at the latter and would otherwise also catch this real,
# tracked source folder. Updated 2026-08-28 when resources/scripts/ moved
# to src/ - the negation is keyed to the literal path, so it silently
# stopped matching anything the moment the directory it names moved,
# with no warning (git just quietly stopped tracking new content there,
# confirmed live: `git add games/caravellius/src` picked up every other
# subfolder except debug/) - a real trap for any future path rename here.
!games/caravellius/src/debug/
!games/caravellius/src/debug/**
**/Release/
**/release/
**/GeneratedFiles/
**/Build/
**/build/
**/CMakeFiles/
**/out/
**/_deps/

# Local, per-developer VSCode config - the tracked source of truth lives in
# docs/vscode/.vscode (see docs/vscode/README.md); copy from there instead
# of editing here directly, so intentional changes don't get lost.
/.vscode/
